    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver: I have gone through the trip record, the GPS trace, the chat export, the fare ledger, both profiles and the missing traffic advisory, and I decide this case on the money.\n\nTHE DEVIATION IS ESTABLISHED AND MATERIAL. Under POL-RD-01 the governing measurement is the GPS trace, which records 30.89 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff events. The trip record's 30.9 km is a rounded convenience copy of the same measurement and may not be cited for the threshold test; nothing turns on the difference here, but the trace figure is the one used. Against the platform's optimal route of 22.10 km stored on the trip record, the excess is 8.79 km, or 39.8% of optimal. Both establishment gates pass (more than 20% of optimal and more than 0.8 km absolute), and because 8.79 km also exceeds the 8.0 km absolute gate the deviation is additionally MATERIAL. The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes: 217 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps, no inter-fix jump over 500 m and no sampling interval over 30 seconds, so POL-RD-07 requires no corroboration and POL-RD-10(3) does not fire.\n\nNO EXCULPATORY CLAUSE APPLIES. POL-RD-03 exonerates only against a traffic advisory that names a road on the optimal route, carries an overlapping validity window and matches a route leaving and rejoining the corridor. The only advisory in the pool, EV-ADVIS-00505-01, is MISSING, has no payload, carries weight 0.0 and fires issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT; it can prove nothing by its content and its absence defeats condition (a). The driver's account that heavy fog on the SLE made him 'go around' is a general assertion about traffic conditions, cites no artifact and no traffic_advisory ID, and under POL-RD-08 it does not discharge the burden that shifted to him once the rider showed a qualifying excess on an unimpaired trace; assertions citing no evidence ID carry no weight. I have also considered whether the absent advisory forces an escalation under POL-RD-10(5), and it does not: that limb is directed at an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, and no artifact was cited here. The minted advisory identifier is a citable absence that defeats exoneration, not a data failure that holds the file. POL-RD-04 fails because the chat log for this trip contains zero messages, so there is no instruction, no timestamp and no waypoint_hint to test. POL-RD-05 fails because no pickup or dropoff amendment was recorded (pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null) and the amended-optimal fields are null with them. POL-RD-12 fails because the vehicle type is RYDE_PLUS, not RYDE_POOL, and solo_optimal_distance_km is null, so 22.10 km is the ordinary booking optimal.\n\nTHE DRIVER-PROFILE CHECK. The material finding requires the POL-RD-06 check. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 250, a ratio of 0.00, so neither limb of the pattern test is met, the FULL_REFUND uplift in POL-RD-06(b) is unavailable and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arises. The driver's rating, account age and lifetime trip count, and the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter, are context only under POL-GEN-01 and ground nothing.\n\nTHE REFUND IS ARITHMETIC. The fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-11 does not displace POL-RD-02. ((3.80 base fare + 0.75 x 22.10 km + 0.28 x 27.0 min) x the surge multiplier of 1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee = a recomputed fare of SGD 28.735. The charged_total is SGD 37.86. Refund = 37.86 - 28.735 = SGD 9.125, rounded UP to SGD 9.15. That is 24.1% of the amount charged - above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and well below the 90% share that would convert the award into a full refund of the fare. No ERP gantries, no tolls and no airport surcharge were charged (correctly, since the surcharge attaches only to trips originating at Changi and this trip ends there), so POL-RD-09 yields no standalone pass-through correction, forbids any double count on top of the figure above, and produces no billing-integrity referral. The billed distance of 30.9 km does not fall short of the trace, so no POL-RD-04 driver compensation is due.\n\nTHE SGD 210 REBOOKING FEE. That sum is not recoverable, and no clause in the loaded policy turns a missed check-in into a refundable line. No artifact in the pool evidences the flight, the rebooking or its cost, and both parties accept that the ruling moves only the fare ledger. The contested amount is therefore the SGD 37.86 charged on EV-FARE-00505.\n\nCONFIDENCE. The deciding facts are carried by artifacts at weight 1.0 (GPS trace, trip record, fare breakdown), so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0; the only impaired artifact, EV-ADVIS-00505-01 at weight 0.0, carries no fact and does not set the cap. I have set confidence at 0.9. One question I leave open for a human reviewer without holding the file: if a road operator or LTA record later confirms a fog or closure event on the SLE corridor between 05:46 and 06:23 on 24 August 2026, the driver's account could be tested under POL-RD-03 on a future reference."
